{
  slug: 'how-to-hard-refresh-any-browser-on-mobile-and-pc-the-right-way',
  title: 'How to Hard Refresh Any Browser on Mobile and PC the RIGHT way',
  date: '2023-07-29',
  sourceUrl: 'https://www.ryanjohnson.website/6007/',
  capturedAt: '2026-07-22',
  excerpt: "tl;dr: You have to access the specific site's cache information by using a button to the left of the URL in your browser. In most browsers, this should be a little lock icon for \"security\". Microsoft Edge and Chrome: Explanation If you're here, you know you're looking at a page that has outdated information and [&hellip;]",
  contentHtml: '<div id="pl-6007"  class="panel-layout" >\n<div id="pg-6007-0"  class="panel-grid panel-no-style" >\n<div id="pgc-6007-0-0"  class="panel-grid-cell"  data-weight="1" >\n<div id="panel-6007-0-0-0" class="so-panel widget widget_text panel-first-child" data-index="0" data-style="{&quot;background_image_attachment&quot;:false,&quot;background_display&quot;:&quot;tile&quot;,&quot;background_image_size&quot;:&quot;full&quot;,&quot;border_thickness&quot;:&quot;1px&quot;}" >\n<div class="textwidget"><strong>tl;dr:</strong> You have to access the specific site&#8217;s cache information by using a button to the left of the URL in your browser. In most browsers, this should be a little lock icon for &#8220;security&#8221;.\n</div>\n</p></div>\n<div id="panel-6007-0-0-1" class="so-panel widget widget_sow-image" data-index="1" data-style="{&quot;background_image_attachment&quot;:false,&quot;background_display&quot;:&quot;tile&quot;,&quot;background_image_size&quot;:&quot;full&quot;,&quot;border_thickness&quot;:&quot;1px&quot;}" ><div\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tclass="so-widget-sow-image so-widget-sow-image-default-8b5b6f678277"\n\t\t\t\n\t\t>\n<div class="sow-image-container">\n\t\t<img \n\tsrc="https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Clear-Cache-Firefox.png" width="673" height="263" srcset="https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Clear-Cache-Firefox.png 673w, https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Clear-Cache-Firefox-500x195.png 500w" sizes="(max-width: 673px) 100vw, 673px" title="Clear Cache Firefox" alt="" \t\tclass="so-widget-image"/>\n\t</div>\n\n</div></div>\n<div id="panel-6007-0-0-2" class="so-panel widget widget_text" data-index="2" data-style="{&quot;background_image_attachment&quot;:false,&quot;background_display&quot;:&quot;tile&quot;,&quot;background_image_size&quot;:&quot;full&quot;,&quot;border_thickness&quot;:&quot;1px&quot;}" >\n<div class="textwidget"><strong>Microsoft Edge and Chrome:</strong></p>\n<p><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-6030" src="https://i0.wp.com/ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Clear-Cache-Chrome.png?resize=500%2C329&#038;ssl=1" alt="" width="500" height="329" data-recalc-dims="1" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Clear-Cache-Chrome.png?w=546&amp;ssl=1 546w, https://i0.wp.com/ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Clear-Cache-Chrome.png?resize=500%2C329&amp;ssl=1 500w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-6029" src="https://i0.wp.com/ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Clear-Cache-Chrome-2.png?resize=372%2C500&#038;ssl=1" alt="" width="372" height="500" data-recalc-dims="1" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Clear-Cache-Chrome-2.png?w=488&amp;ssl=1 488w, https://i0.wp.com/ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Clear-Cache-Chrome-2.png?resize=372%2C500&amp;ssl=1 372w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 372px) 100vw, 372px" />\n</div>\n</p></div>\n<div id="panel-6007-0-0-3" class="so-panel widget widget_text panel-last-child" data-index="3" data-style="{&quot;background_image_attachment&quot;:false,&quot;background_display&quot;:&quot;tile&quot;,&quot;background_image_size&quot;:&quot;full&quot;,&quot;border_thickness&quot;:&quot;1px&quot;}" >\n<h3 class="widget-title">Explanation</h3>\n<div class="textwidget">If you&#8217;re here, you know you&#8217;re looking at a page that has outdated information and you need to refresh the content, but for some reason, it won&#8217;t show up for you. This is because browsers will cache (save) information so they don&#8217;t have to download it repeatedly when visiting a website multiple times. Unfortunately, this means the website may have new information, but the browser, being the one in control, doesnt&#8217; request it, assuming it knows everything. Narcissism much, browser?</p>\n<p>Here&#8217;s how to clear the cache THE RIGHT WAY. There is a right way and a wrong way. Most everyone tells you to do this the wrong way. Whenever I talk to technical support personnel, they want me to &#8220;clear my browser cache&#8221;. Well, you know what? That&#8217;s rude. EXTREMELY rude. I&#8217;ve pointed out a mistake on your website, and your first thought is to have me clear all of the data for every website I&#8217;ve ever visited? I&#8217;m logged in to about 200 different websites, at least! I don&#8217;t have all day to waste on re-logging, just because you had a hunch! And, on top of that, the &#8220;browser cache&#8221; theory is almost always wrong, for me. Maybe, perhaps on a global scale, other people do have this problem, but when I run into website problems, this is one of the first things I&#8217;ve already considered. By the time a tech support person hears from me, I&#8217;ve already tested this, usually. So, in the interest of making tech support nicer to people, I&#8217;ve been wanting to post this for a long time&#8211;I just didn&#8217;t know it. I&#8217;ve been giving these same instructions to support people for years, and never considered putting it in my blog, but here we are. Finally, the pieces click together.</p>\n<p>Even most websites that tell you how to clear your cache tell you to do some convoluted dive into the browser&#8217;s settings, such as this article at <a href="https://techwiser.com/hard-refresh-any-browser-mobile-pc/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://techwiser.com/hard-refresh-any-browser-mobile-pc/</a>. In Firefox, this works, but it&#8217;s inefficient. In Chrome and Microsoft Edge, however, this is straight up wrong. The only option in settings is to clear the <em>entire</em> cache, which will ruin your day.</p>\n<p>For more no-bullshit tech advice and discussions, follow my blog.\n</p></div>\n</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n',
  wordpressId: 6007,
}
